.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-GRANT-NAMESPACE-ACCESS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-grant-namespace-access \- grant a user access to a namespace within an account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam grant-namespace-access
.BR \-\-user | \-u
.I ERN
.BR \-\-account\-id | \-a
.I ACCOUNTID
.BR \-\-namespace | \-s
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Grants a user explicit access to one namespace within one account via the
eam service's
.I grant-namespace-access
action.
.PP
The caller must be a global administrator, or already hold account-scoped
administrator privileges on \fIACCOUNTID\fR.
.PP
Access is granted per (account, namespace) pair, not per account: a user
may hold grants across several accounts, and within each account, only
for the specific namespaces it has been explicitly granted - granting
\fIdevelopment\fR does not implicitly grant \fIproduction\fR. Both
\fIACCOUNTID\fR and the namespace named by \fB\-\-namespace\fR must
already exist (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-account (1)
and
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-namespace (1)).
.PP
This is unrelated to global administrator status, which is instead
membership in the
.I administrator
user group (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-user-group-add-user (1)).
A global administrator already bypasses every grant check.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIERN\fR
ERN of the user to grant access to. Required.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account\-id " " \fIACCOUNTID\fR
Account the namespace belongs to. Required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-namespace " " \fINAME\fR
Namespace within \fIACCOUNTID\fR to grant access to. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The grant was created.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller
lacks administrator privileges on the account, the namespace or user does
not exist, or the user already holds this grant. If the failure was an
expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file
is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam grant-namespace-access \e
    --user ern:euclid:eam:eu-central-1:123456789012:user:jdoe \e
    --account-id 123456789012 --namespace development
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-revoke-namespace-access (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-namespace (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-account (1)
